  "goodToKnow": "Der Vorfahr (die Vorfahrin) is an ancestor, usually in the plural: meine Vorfahren. It's a weak noun: den Vorfahren. The opposite is die Nachkommen (descendants). Literally, the Vorfahren are those who went (fahren, in its old meaning to go) before (vor) us. Die Ahnenforschung (genealogy) is a popular hobby in Germany. Don't confuse it with die Vorfahrt (right of way)."
